1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:22,590
The morning after my graduation, a nigga tried to rob a casino while I
was buying coffee in uniform. That was his first mistake. His second
was parking in front of my Lamborghini. I stood outside the coffee
shop with two cups in my hands. Shawna sat in the passenger seat
wearing sunglasses and my captain's jacket over her dress.

2
00:00:22,840 --> 00:00:42,613
She'd taken it off me because she said the gold braid felt good
against her wrists. Nigga, the department hadn't had time to miss it
yet. Across the street, four men came out of a casino carrying bags.
Behind them an alarm rang. One man had a gun pointed backward toward
the doors.

3
00:00:42,863 --> 00:01:05,551
Another had a bleeding lip and a look that suggested he had expected
the morning to involve less resistance. Their van stood across my
bumper. I looked at the coffee. Looked at the van. Looked at Shawna.
"Baby, hold these." She took both cups. "You getting involved?" "Nigga
involved me when he parked." The driver saw me coming and laughed.

4
00:01:05,801 --> 00:01:27,578
"Keep walking, pretty boy." I opened my shirt enough for him to see
the badge. His laugh changed shape. "Police?" "Captain." "You don't
look like police." "Nigga, police improving. Move the van." The man
behind him raised his pistol. I caught the van's open door and drove
it into his arm. The shot went into the street.

5
00:01:27,828 --> 00:01:50,719
I hit him against the side panel and took him down while the driver
tried to get back behind the wheel. The van lurched forward. Its rear
doors were still open. Bags of money tumbled out. The driver shouted
at his partner to pull them in, and I caught the door handle as the
van gathered speed. "Aiden!" Shawna shouted. "Coffee!" I shouted back.

6
00:01:50,969 --> 00:02:08,869
I wasn't going to let some nigga make her spill eight dollars on a
police uniform. The van dragged me past the corner. My shoes hit the
curb, found it, lost it. I got one foot on the rear step and pulled
myself up while the man inside tried to kick me off.

7
00:02:09,119 --> 00:02:28,465
"Nigga, let go!" "You let go!" "It's my van!" "Then your nigga
should've moved it!" I came through the doors and hit him into the
pile of bags. The driver looked back. That was enough to put the van
halfway onto the sidewalk. A newspaper stand exploded against the
windshield.

8
00:02:28,715 --> 00:02:52,712
Papers flew everywhere, yesterday's miracles suddenly competing with
the one hanging out of a moving fucking robbery. The man on the floor
reached for his gun. I put my foot on his wrist. "Don't." He looked up
at me. "You're Aiden." "Nigga, you would've had a easier day
remembering that at the coffee shop." The driver turned into a parking
structure. Concrete closed over us.

9
00:02:52,962 --> 00:03:12,215
Tires screamed on the first ramp. The van tipped, caught, and kept
climbing. I could hear my Lamborghini outside before I saw it. Shawna
came through the entrance behind us with the siren on. My jacket was
back over the seat. The coffee cups sat upright in the holders.

10
00:03:12,464 --> 00:03:30,737
My woman was chasing a van full of criminals while saving my
breakfast, and nigga, every good thing I'd ever believed about
marriage started taking notes. We hit the second floor. Then the
third. The driver shouted, "She's still behind us!" "She's thorough,"
I told him.

11
00:03:30,987 --> 00:03:51,532
"Nigga, who the fuck asked you?" "You brought me." At the next turn,
Shawna swung the Lamborghini across the ramp above us and stopped. The
driver braked. The van slid. I caught the front seat before I went
through it, and the two men behind me hit the bags of money in a way
that sounded financially painful.

12
00:03:51,782 --> 00:04:13,299
Shawna got out with her silver pistol in her hand. "Everybody out."
The driver stared through the windshield. "She's police too?" "Nigga,
she's worse. She's disappointed." He put up his hands. Knox's officers
found us on the third floor ten minutes later. Four men on the ground.
The stolen money in the van.

13
00:04:13,549 --> 00:04:36,670
My Lamborghini blocking the ramp like the city had finally bought
itself a beautiful fucking answer. A sergeant with a gray mustache
shook my hand so hard I had to tell him about the coffee. "Captain, we
have been after that crew for months." "Niggas parked wrong." He
looked at the van, then back at me. "We should've tried that." Shawna
handed me my cup.

14
00:04:36,920 --> 00:04:57,177
Still warm. Not one fucking drop on the seat. The sergeant saluted her
too. "Ma'am." "You can call me Shawna." "Yes, ma'am." Nigga, respect
sometimes refused to take a suggestion. The casino owner came to the
station before lunch. He brought two gold watches and an envelope.

15
00:04:57,427 --> 00:05:18,444
I gave the watches to the two employees the robbers had knocked down,
kept the envelope because gratitude ought to reach its address, and
bought the whole shift lunch with it. Knox watched from her office
doorway while officers took pictures beside my car. "How's your first
morning?" "Need a bigger cup holder." She laughed.

16
00:05:18,694 --> 00:05:40,403
"Anything else?" "Nigga wants a raise." "You've been here four hours."
"And look what the four hours did for you." By evening every officer
in the station knew my name. By the next afternoon, when I went to buy
the suit for Red's gala, half of them had volunteered to wait outside
the Saint in case my night needed company.

17
00:05:40,653 --> 00:05:59,309
I told them to stay close to Knox. Red liked surprises. I intended to
give the nigga one wearing a badge. I bought a white suit for the
robbery because I wanted Red to see who ruined his fucking life. The
tailor tried to sell me black. Then he tried to sell me dark blue.

18
00:05:59,559 --> 00:06:20,803
He had Shawna on a little velvet chair behind me, drinking champagne
and telling him I looked handsome in everything, which meant she
hadn't looked up from her phone once. Nigga, white, I told him. I want
the whole room seeing who came. Your injury— Nigga, is the suit going
to heal me? The nigga stopped talking about the injury.

19
00:06:21,053 --> 00:06:42,983
Tank stood beside the door in a black suit we had bought forty minutes
earlier. He had already torn it reaching for a peppermint. The tailor
was pretending not to notice. I wasn't. Get the nigga another one too.
A larger size? Get that nigga whatever size a cathedral is. Tank put
the peppermint back. Nigga, eat.

20
00:06:43,233 --> 00:07:06,200
We rich enough for the candy and whatever seam your ass takes with it.
Shawna laughed then. She lifted her eyes, and for a second I had her.
No dead husband. No diamond. No Red waiting for his chance. Just my
woman laughing because I was standing in a thousand pins threatening
to buy a church-sized suit for the biggest motherfucker in Nevada.

21
00:07:06,450 --> 00:07:26,962
My nigga, I would've bought the actual church to keep her laughing.
Between graduating, becoming a captain, and chasing a van through a
parking garage, I had still found time for the three days before the
gala to do something terrible to me. I could take a bullet. I could
bury a man who called himself my father.

22
00:07:27,212 --> 00:07:45,068
But sitting beside Shawna while she told Red over the phone that she
missed him had me walking around my own house like I was looking for
somebody to rob. I knew the plan. Nigga, I had agreed to the plan. I
had nodded while she explained it and said some shit about trusting
her.

23
00:07:45,318 --> 00:08:05,944
Then she had put Red on speaker and called him baby, and all that
intelligent shit left my body. You don't have to say it to that nigga
like that, I told her afterward. Like what? With your mouth. She
stared at me. Aiden. Nigga got a name. Use the name. She hung up on
the argument by kissing me. I let her.

24
00:08:06,194 --> 00:08:26,252
The second night I made the same complaint, and she kissed me again.
By the third, she knew exactly what I was doing and told me to come
over there without starting a fight first. Now the tailor knelt beside
my shoes while she answered another message. That nigga again? Rosa.
Let me see. She turned the screen.

25
00:08:26,502 --> 00:08:46,682
Rosa had sent a picture of six gowns thrown across a bed and the words
Your nigga paying for all this? Tell her your nigga said yes. You
don't know how much it is. Tell her yes in capital fucking letters.
Shawna put her phone away. Then she stood and walked around the tailor
to straighten my collar herself.

26
00:08:46,932 --> 00:09:08,417
You know you're allowed to be scared tonight. I'm not. Okay. You are?
Yes. I caught her wrist before she could step away. Dante's watch slid
down against my fingers. I let it. Then your nigga scared too. She
kissed the uncut corner of my mouth. Good. Maybe you'll listen. I
listened to every fucking thing she said.

27
00:09:08,668 --> 00:09:30,832
I just sometimes decided the whole world was wrong after I heard it.
At the house, Rosa had turned our bedroom into a kingdom of women
getting dressed. There were shoes on the chairs, perfume in the air,
and a bottle of champagne standing in the sink beside my toothbrush.
Somebody had moved my gun to make room for a heated hairbrush.

28
00:09:31,082 --> 00:09:53,817
Nigga, I owned the house, and they asked me why I was in there. Nigga,
because I sleep here. Not while we're busy, Rosa said. She was wearing
red, diamonds at her throat, and an expression that told me she had
already decided who was going to disappoint her that night. I need
Shawna. Your nigga needs patience, Rosa told Shawna. Nigga, I bought
patience.

29
00:09:54,067 --> 00:10:06,982
They said it'll be here tomorrow. Rosa picked up a shoe. A nigga left.
Downstairs, Marcellus sat by the windows in a gray suit. Somebody had
polished his shoes until they looked wet.

30
00:10:07,232 --> 00:10:28,921
The disguise was supposed to make him a wealthy old jeweler, which
mostly involved getting him a better jacket and telling him not to
look like he wanted Red dragged behind a car. My nigga still looked
like that. On the table in front of him lay Celeste's letter. The
folds were so worn they looked ready to separate. He wasn't reading
it.

31
00:10:29,171 --> 00:10:49,444
He had laid one hand across the paper like somebody might reach down
from heaven and take it back. My nigga, tell me you ready, I said. I
have been ready for years. Nigga, that's not what I asked. He looked
up, and for the first time since I met him, the old man almost smiled.
Yes, Aiden. I sat across from him.

32
00:10:49,694 --> 00:11:12,127
My side objected. That bullet had settled into my life like it
intended to pay rent. Every time I forgot it, the pain came back to
tell me who had put it there. Marcellus glanced at the way I lowered
myself. Does she know how much that hurts? She knows everything. Does
she? I looked toward the stairs. Nigga, she knows enough.

33
00:11:12,377 --> 00:11:35,280
He folded Celeste's letter and put it in his inside pocket. The stone
cannot love you back, he said. I got somebody for that. Then remember
which one you came for. Before I could answer, Tank walked in holding
two phones. He turned one facedown as soon as he saw us. Niggas, the
cars ready. What nigga calling you? Nobody.

34
00:11:35,529 --> 00:11:55,405
Nigga, then why you got two phones? In case somebody does. I would've
laughed on any other night. That night I watched him put both in his
pocket, and something in my stomach moved. I thought about asking
again. Then I heard Shawna on the stairs. My nigga, everything in me
turned around. She wore blue.

35
00:11:55,655 --> 00:12:13,877
Dark blue, cut close to her body, with a train dragging behind her
like even the floor wanted to hold on. Diamonds touched her ears.
Dante's watch was on her wrist. Her hair was up, and that little scar
above her eyebrow stood out plainly. I loved the scar.

36
00:12:14,127 --> 00:12:35,330
I loved knowing the exact place on her face where the world had tried
some shit and failed. Rosa's dress, she said when she saw me looking.
She never wore it. Nigga, I said I'd buy you anything. I wanted this
one. Rosa lifted the train off the last stair. And I want it back.
Both of you hear me? Yes, Shawna said.

37
00:12:35,580 --> 00:13:00,125
I should've heard how softly she said it. Rosa came down behind her
carrying a small envelope. I've got the watch paper, she said. The
original. Nobody gets it off me. The order hidden in Dante's watch was
inside. Red's words. Red's decision. All the grief he had handed
Shawna while pretending he was helping her carry it. Shawna had made a
copy for tonight.

38
00:13:00,375 --> 00:13:20,537
Rosa would keep the original safe, along with the truth if none of us
came back. I didn't like thinking about that second part, so I stood
up. Turn around for your nigga, I told Shawna. She did. Again. Aiden.
Nigga, I'm trying to remember whether there's anybody left alive I
need to thank.

39
00:13:20,787 --> 00:13:37,331
She slipped her little silver pistol into her purse, then came over
and put both hands against my chest. If you tear this dress, I'm
killing you before Red gets the chance. Your nigga will buy the
factory. I'll kill you in the factory. I kissed her.

40
00:13:37,581 --> 00:14:01,821
I kissed her until Tank cleared his throat, then I kissed her again
because that nigga did not determine the length of my happiness. We
went to the Saint in four cars. I drove Shawna in the dark-blue police
Lamborghini. Tank kept the original black Mercedes behind us. Rosa
drove Marcellus, and Porsche brought Mercedes in the green Bentley. I
wanted six.

41
00:14:02,071 --> 00:14:21,134
Tank said we only had enough people for four. I told him to put one
nigga in each of the other two, and he asked who was driving.
Apparently the man had chosen tonight to become a fucking
mathematician. Four cars pulled under the Saint's canopy. Four cars
full of my niggas.

42
00:14:21,384 --> 00:14:40,328
It still looked like a palace somebody had built with all the money
they should've used to raise their children. Gold everywhere. Flowers
as tall as men. A fountain full of coins that were worth less than one
button on the security guard's jacket. Red had made the gala white
tie.

43
00:14:40,578 --> 00:15:02,999
Nigga thought if he dressed his sins in enough silk, God might mistake
them for somebody else's. I came out in my white suit with the cross
against my chest, the captain's badge inside my jacket, and Shawna
beside me. Cameras started flashing. My nigga, that surprised me. I
had expected guns. Keep walking, she whispered.

44
00:15:03,249 --> 00:15:27,131
I kept walking like I had paid for the fucking sidewalk. A
photographer asked us to stop against a wall of white roses. Shawna
put her hand on my shoulder. I put mine at her waist. A man with a
microphone asked whether I was taking over Big T's interests. Every
nigga that owes them anything owes me, I said. And your relationship
with Mr.

45
00:15:27,381 --> 00:15:50,972
Redmond? Redmond. Nigga had a government name tonight. Ask me at the
end. Rosa stepped between the reporter and us before I could make it
worse. Tank followed so closely I felt his jacket brush mine. For a
second his hand touched my arm. Anything happen tonight, he said, you
stay with me. Nigga, that was already the idea. The nigga didn't
answer.

46
00:15:51,222 --> 00:16:11,982
Inside, a staircase curved around a statue of a naked woman holding a
bowl of fire. Red had put real flames in the bowl. I respected that
nigga for that one thing. If you were going to waste money, make the
building itself nervous. Women in jewels walked past women who had
sold them drugs in the bathroom.

47
00:16:12,232 --> 00:16:33,661
Men greeted men they had paid to have killed and had not yet heard
back about. A preacher I recognized from television stood beside a man
whose entire fortune came from stolen cars. The preacher had the
bigger watch. There was a private lounge full of cocaine and
champagne. Somebody called my name from inside.

48
00:16:33,910 --> 00:16:56,284
I looked over and saw a man I had spent a filthy weekend with before I
ever met Shawna, sitting between two women I had met the same weekend.
He lifted his glass. Aiden! You disappear when you fall in love?
Nigga, I got promoted. The women laughed. Shawna looked at all three,
then at me. All of them? Your nigga had a long weekend.

49
00:16:56,534 --> 00:17:19,448
You nasty motherfucker. You love me. She squeezed my hand hard enough
to hurt. Don't get confident. I got confident. I got so fucking
confident that when Red came down the far staircase in a dark green
jacket, I smiled at him like he had arrived at my party. He wasn't
looking at me. He was looking at Shawna. There she is, Red said.

50
00:17:19,698 --> 00:17:42,234
Nigga sounded like she had come out of his own prayers. He held out
both hands. She gave him one. He kissed it above Dante's watch. Nigga,
I saw the whole murder happen in my mind. His head through the flower
arrangement. His green jacket on fire. Me standing over him while the
preacher told God to mind His business. Instead I smiled.

51
00:17:42,484 --> 00:18:04,416
Nigga, you throw a good party. Shame about your future. Red finally
looked at me. Captain, Red said, and the word came out like a bone he
had to swallow. You clean up well. You still talking. Shawna's fingers
tightened against my arm. Red laughed softly, as if I was a child who
had threatened to buy his own house. We should get a photograph.

52
00:18:04,666 --> 00:18:27,182
All three of us. Before anybody could object, he called the
photographer over. He put Shawna in the middle. Then he rested a hand
against her upper arm. On that hand he wore a broad dark ring with a
blue stone set almost flush into it. Marcellus, a few feet behind us,
went perfectly still at the sight of Red holding Shawna.

53
00:18:27,432 --> 00:18:49,454
The ring was half-hidden against the green sleeve. The flash went off.
The nigga asked for another. I stared straight into the lens. If that
photograph ever hung in a museum, people would know which motherfucker
had come there to kill somebody. An attendant brought glossy little
copies while Red greeted Rosa. Rosa took two.

54
00:18:49,704 --> 00:19:11,154
She tucked them into her purse with a smile I knew cost her real
effort. Now, Red said, holding out his arm to Shawna, I promised this
woman a dance. Shawna looked at me. I remembered every word of the
plan. I remembered agreeing. I remembered her saying she needed him
close and foolish and thinking he had already won.

55
00:19:11,404 --> 00:19:27,246
I also remembered that I had hands. One dance, I said. Red smiled.
Let's see what she wants. Then he took my woman onto the floor, and I
followed them with my eyes like a nigga watching his own heart get
carried through traffic.
